# Build products generated in place by the XP build scripts
# (build_python_xp.bat / build_tcltk_xp.bat / Tools/xp/*).
# Sources stay in git. libffi-3.4.4/win32 is re-included on purpose: it
# holds the XP-built runtime the layout tree and the installer consume
# (libffi-8.dll), and libffi is never relinked by the build scripts, so
# the copies never go stale. tcltk-9.0.4.0/win32 keeps only headers,
# import libs / script libs and the two shells in git: build_tcltk_xp.bat
# relinks tcl90.dll / tcl9tk90.dll on every run and copy /y overwrites
# the bin\ copies (fresh builds left the tree dirty, 2026-10-25), so the
# bin DLLs are now build products and must be regenerated by
# build_tcltk_xp.bat after a fresh clone.
!libffi-3.4.4/win32/**
!tcltk-9.0.4.0/win32/include/**
!tcltk-9.0.4.0/win32/lib/**
!tcltk-9.0.4.0/win32/bin/*.exe
tcltk-9.0.4.0/win32/bin/*.dll

# WiX 3.14 toolchain itself ships here: candle.exe/light.exe/wix.dll/
# burn.exe are required by build_msi_xp.bat, and WiX 3.14 is no longer
# downloadable from its original home - without these files a fresh
# clone cannot build the installers at all.
!windows-installer/wix-314/**/*.exe
!windows-installer/wix-314/**/*.dll

# object files / link intermediates generated anywhere in the trees
**/*.obj
**/*.res
**/*.d

# openssl: 2000+ in-tree objects from nmake, plus the built runtime
openssl-3.5.9-src/*.dll
openssl-3.5.9-src/*.lib
openssl-3.5.9-src/*.pdb
openssl-3.5.9-src/*.exe

# tcl/tk: nmake output directories (also inside the bundled pkgs/) and
# the helper executables they build.  nmakehlp.out is nmakehlp.exe's
# cache holding OUT_DIR/TMP_DIR as absolute paths - machine specific, so
# it must not be tracked.
tcl-9.0.4.0/**/Release_VC*/
**/nmakehlp.exe
**/nmakehlp.out
tk-9.0.4.1/**/Release_VC*/

openssl-3.5.9-src/depend

# openssl build stamp (see build_openssl_xp.bat)
openssl-3.5.9-src/.xp_build_ok

# tcl 9.0.4 tarball ships prebuilt zlib/tommath DLLs the nmake files have
# NO rule to regenerate (16-test fresh-clone finding: nmake died on the
# missing zlib1.dll input) - the root *.dll rule had silently dropped them
!tcl-9.0.4.0/compat/zlib/win32/zlib1.dll
!tcl-9.0.4.0/libtommath/win32/libtommath.dll
